{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Undefined Rational Expression.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Undefined Rational Expression.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"undefined rational expression undefined rational expression","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Undefined Rational Expression.md","fileName":"Undefined Rational Expression.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Undefined Rational Expression","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Polynomial and Rational Expressions]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial and Rational Expressions","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Undefined Rational Expression.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Undefined Rational Expression.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"undefined rational expression undefined rational expression","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Undefined Rational Expression.md","fileName":"Undefined Rational Expression.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Undefined Rational Expression","heading":"Undefined Rational Expression","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A rational expression is undefined at any value that makes its denominator zero. Before simplifying\n\n$$\\frac{x^2-1}{x-1},$$\n\nthe value (x=1) must be excluded. Factoring and cancelling gives (x+1), but the original expression still has no value at (x=1).\n\nRestrictions should therefore be identified before cancellation, multiplication, or cross multiplication. A transformation can preserve equality only on the domain where every expression and division used in the step is defined.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial and Rational Expressions","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Undefined Rational Expression.m